  "notes": "**Hutsix v3.9.0**(released)\n\n### Profile Manager\n- **Fixed: a profile could not be created from an executable chosen with Browse\u2026.** The choice vanished the next time the running-app list refreshed (about once a second), so Create reported \"Choose the app first\" even though you had just picked one. The browsed app now stays in the list and is used for the profile.\n- **Fixed: clicking a binding no longer traps the form in editing.** Selecting a binding only arms Delete; to edit one, double-click it. The form returns to \"Add Binding\" after you save an edit, so you can keep adding bindings instead of being stuck on the last one.\n- **Fixed: the binding list now refreshes when you switch to a different profile.** It kept showing the previous profile's bindings until something else happened to reload it.\n\n### Triggers\n- **Fixed: calibrating a text trigger from a captured area now keeps the area you drew.** It used to shrink the saved area to where the template was found, so the trigger watched a tiny box instead of the region you selected. The template still pins *which* text to watch; it just no longer overrides your chosen area.\n- **Fixed: the \"Choose Image\" button now enables reliably when you switch to calibrating from an image file.**\n- **A text trigger can now track a moving element.** Tick **\"The element can move \u2014 track it\"** during calibration and Hutsix re-finds the element as it runs (on a throttled cadence) instead of watching one fixed spot \u2014 useful when the thing you're reading drifts around a region of the screen.",
